1
00:00:03,803 --> 00:00:05,538
Let's disinfect our hands again.

2
00:00:05,605 --> 00:00:06,439
Okay.

3
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:13,580
I thought you would take me to
a sushi place that's like a sterile room.

4
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:16,883
This place is safer than a sterile room.

5
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:17,851
Really?

6
00:00:17,917 --> 00:00:20,520
Viruses have existed
for three billion years

7
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:23,957
and fish for 400 million years.

8
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:25,492
They're much older than us.

9
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:27,460
This all looks so good!

10
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:29,829
So what will you start with?

11
00:00:31,731 --> 00:00:33,199
- Octopus.
- Octopus, please.

12
00:00:35,969 --> 00:00:37,270
Okay. Octopus.

13
00:00:37,837 --> 00:00:39,372
- Do you like octopus?
- Yes!

14
00:00:40,774 --> 00:00:43,476
Dr. Hachisuka always starts
with octopus too.

15
00:00:44,244 --> 00:00:45,645
Is there anything you don't like?

16
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:48,314
No. I love all kinds of sushi!

17
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,051
Eat as much as you like.

18
00:00:51,651 --> 00:00:52,485
Okay!

19
00:00:53,019 --> 00:00:54,454
Here goes!

20
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:02,195
And after the octopus?

21
00:01:04,164 --> 00:01:05,598
Let's see…

22
00:01:06,266 --> 00:01:07,333
<i>Kohada,</i> please.

23
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,637
I also love both octopus and <i>kohada,</i>
but feel free to order

24
00:01:10,703 --> 00:01:12,205
more expensive fish.

25
00:01:12,272 --> 00:01:13,339
- Really?
- Sure.

26
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:14,741
If you insist.

27
00:01:16,643 --> 00:01:20,080
Fatty tuna! Urchin! Roe! Sea bream!

28
00:01:20,146 --> 00:01:23,016
Also abalone and <i>amaebi!</i>

29
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:25,285
Plus eel. Do you have <i>nodoguro?</i>

30
00:01:25,351 --> 00:01:26,553
Sure.

31
00:01:39,065 --> 00:01:42,902
I was going to celebrate alone today.

32
00:01:46,005 --> 00:01:47,273
Before long,

33
00:01:47,874 --> 00:01:49,676
physicians worldwide will unite

34
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:54,080
across borders, cultures, and religions,

35
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:58,084
to complete the Infection Research Center.

36
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:00,453
My ideal…

37
00:02:01,554 --> 00:02:05,458
100% perfect treatment will be realized.

38
00:02:08,661 --> 00:02:10,497
My talk must be boring you.

39
00:02:12,031 --> 00:02:13,800
What's next?

40
00:02:14,901 --> 00:02:17,103
Of course, I have my next plans ready!

41
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:19,472
Instead of fighting viruses,
we'll co-exist with them.

42
00:02:20,073 --> 00:02:24,444
Viruses aren't just harmful.
They can be used to treat cancer.

43
00:02:24,511 --> 00:02:25,345
I've decided!

44
00:02:26,379 --> 00:02:29,048
Next, I'll have octopus, <i>kohada,</i> and…

45
00:02:29,549 --> 00:02:31,284
- And?
- And…

46
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:34,821
Fatty tuna! Urchin! Roe! Sea bream!

47
00:02:34,888 --> 00:02:35,989
Abalone! <i>Amaebi!</i>

48
00:02:36,556 --> 00:02:38,091
One more round, sir!

49
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,459
Coming right up.

50
00:02:40,193 --> 00:02:43,062
- You must be hungry after surgery.
- Yes!

51
00:02:44,197 --> 00:02:46,933
SUSHI JUBEI

52
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,801
I'm stuffed!

53
00:02:49,469 --> 00:02:51,404
That was delicious!

54
00:02:52,539 --> 00:02:54,107
This is a great restaurant.

55
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:57,877
I'm glad it wasn't a sterile room.

56
00:03:01,548 --> 00:03:02,982
- Do you have it?
- Certainly.

57
00:03:04,484 --> 00:03:05,919
It's ready.

58
00:03:08,388 --> 00:03:11,391
This is for Mr. Kambara.

59
00:03:11,457 --> 00:03:14,427
It's thanks
for all the melons he has given me.

60
00:03:14,494 --> 00:03:15,461
Seriously?

61
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:17,630
Akira will love this! Thank you.

62
00:03:19,132 --> 00:03:21,301
I'll take care of the bill. Go on ahead.

63
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,736
Really? Well, if you insist. Thank you.

64
00:03:24,504 --> 00:03:26,105
Thanks for the food.

65
00:03:26,172 --> 00:03:27,407
Thank you.

66
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:31,511
You didn't eat much today, Dr. Hachisuka.

67
00:03:32,178 --> 00:03:35,582
Dr. Daimon ate enough for me.

68
00:03:36,182 --> 00:03:37,317
Right.

69
00:03:38,418 --> 00:03:39,619
Okay.

70
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:43,122
- Put it on this.
- Thank you.

71
00:03:43,189 --> 00:03:44,090
One moment, please.

72
00:03:58,338 --> 00:04:01,507
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

73
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:04,744
<i>2021.</i>

74
00:04:05,345 --> 00:04:08,448
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

75
00:04:08,514 --> 00:04:10,917
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

76
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:15,822
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

77
00:04:15,888 --> 00:04:19,092
<i>have somehow weathered the storm.</i>

78
00:04:19,826 --> 00:04:21,427
Good morning.

79
00:04:21,494 --> 00:04:25,698
Medical Solutions Headquarters Chief
Hachisuka will now conduct

80
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:29,202
the combined Internal Medicine
and Surgery meeting.

81
00:04:30,570 --> 00:04:32,205
Good morning, everyone!

82
00:04:35,174 --> 00:04:37,710
Good morning, Surgery personnel.

83
00:04:38,544 --> 00:04:40,113
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

84
00:04:41,514 --> 00:04:44,384
Good morning, Acting Director Hiruma.

85
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:47,053
Oh, good morning.

86
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,255
Today's meeting could have been online,

87
00:04:49,322 --> 00:04:53,059
but Chief Hachisuka
has an important announcement today.

88
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,128
Really? An important announcement?

89
00:04:55,728 --> 00:04:57,130
Let's have a listen.

90
00:04:57,196 --> 00:04:58,031
Before that,

91
00:04:58,097 --> 00:04:59,799
let me introduce someone.

92
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,934
Don't ignore the Acting Director!

93
00:05:02,001 --> 00:05:06,172
Director of the Safiristan Kingdom's
Infection Research Center

94
00:05:06,239 --> 00:05:07,974
and a member of the WHO,

95
00:05:09,208 --> 00:05:10,710
Professor Shelp!

96
00:05:10,777 --> 00:05:12,712
PROFESSOR SHELP, SAFIRISTAN KINGDOM
INFECTION RESEARCH CENTER DIRECTOR

97
00:05:37,136 --> 00:05:38,538
Hey!

98
00:05:38,604 --> 00:05:40,406
Quit getting all carried away in English!

99
00:05:41,307 --> 00:05:43,609
Would you please explain
in simple Japanese

100
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:45,978
for those doctors over there?

101
00:05:47,613 --> 00:05:49,482
I am terribly sorry.

102
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:52,352
The novel coronavirus won't be

103
00:05:52,418 --> 00:05:57,590
the last virus that could emerge
somewhere in the world.

104
00:05:58,624 --> 00:06:02,028
The work of preventing
infectious diseases never ends!

105
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:06,866
Therefore, to proactively prevent
the next pandemic,

106
00:06:07,467 --> 00:06:11,904
we will establish in our hospital
a treatment facility…

107
00:06:15,174 --> 00:06:17,477
The Infection Research Center!

108
00:06:20,113 --> 00:06:21,114
Hold on!

109
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,815
Hold on a second!

110
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:27,687
Since when did Totei University Hospital
become your hospital?

111
00:06:27,754 --> 00:06:28,855
That's right!

112
00:06:28,921 --> 00:06:31,257
Is he really building
his own Tower of Babel?

113
00:06:31,858 --> 00:06:34,227
And where did the money
for this come from?

114
00:06:34,293 --> 00:06:38,030
I heard a foreign pharmaceutical company
invested a ton of money.

115
00:06:38,097 --> 00:06:38,931
Seriously?

116
00:06:38,998 --> 00:06:42,435
I also have one more
important announcement

117
00:06:42,935 --> 00:06:45,037
for you, Acting Director Hiruma.

118
00:06:46,472 --> 00:06:51,577
After consulting with
Hospital Director McCartney in the US,

119
00:06:53,045 --> 00:06:58,851
the tenure of hospital administrators
will be limited.

120
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:00,620
Hey! Why are you doing that?

121
00:07:01,487 --> 00:07:04,524
A concentration of power
leads to corruption.

122
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:05,425
From now on,

123
00:07:05,491 --> 00:07:07,827
tenure for all administrators,

124
00:07:07,894 --> 00:07:10,163
besides the director,
will be limited to one year!

125
00:07:10,229 --> 00:07:11,063
What?

126
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:13,766
I thought Acting Director Hiruma
had made a comeback,

127
00:07:13,833 --> 00:07:15,635
but he has to quit after this year?

128
00:07:15,701 --> 00:07:18,471
In other words,
they're kicking out Dr. Hiruma.

129
00:07:18,538 --> 00:07:21,507
- Kicking out Dr. Hiruma?
- Kicking out Dr. Hiruma?

130
00:07:26,145 --> 00:07:27,814
I wasn't told of this.

131
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,282
Hey! Take that back!

132
00:07:29,849 --> 00:07:32,752
No matter how much you may insist,

133
00:07:32,819 --> 00:07:35,054
Totei University Hospital

134
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:39,292
won't follow your orders
for a single moment.

135
00:07:39,358 --> 00:07:40,393
- Understand?
- That's right!

136
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:41,961
Take that back!

137
00:07:42,028 --> 00:07:43,996
That's right! Take it back!

138
00:07:44,063 --> 00:07:46,632
This meeting is now over!

139
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:51,737
Hey, Dr. Hachisuka! Stop right there!

140
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:55,074
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

141
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:57,743
<i>this freelance maverick doctor</i>

142
00:07:57,810 --> 00:08:01,814
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

143
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:05,084
<i>She hates groups,</i>

144
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:07,720
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

145
00:08:07,787 --> 00:08:09,088
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

146
00:08:09,589 --> 00:08:12,959
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

147
00:08:13,025 --> 00:08:14,026
<i>to work her way up.</i>

148
00:08:15,595 --> 00:08:18,364
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

149
00:08:18,431 --> 00:08:21,467
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

150
00:08:50,897 --> 00:08:54,300
How disrespectful
that damn infection maniac is!

151
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:57,937
Who does he think he is?

152
00:08:58,004 --> 00:08:58,838
That's right!

153
00:08:59,438 --> 00:09:01,173
He's not only taking over this hospital,

154
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,975
he's globalizing it too!

155
00:09:03,042 --> 00:09:04,477
I won't stand for it!

156
00:09:06,078 --> 00:09:07,880
You have a visitor,
Acting Director Hiruma.

157
00:09:07,947 --> 00:09:08,948
Can't you see we're busy?

158
00:09:09,515 --> 00:09:10,816
It's your wife, sir.

159
00:09:13,786 --> 00:09:15,855
Sorry to bother you at work.

160
00:09:15,922 --> 00:09:17,690
What's the matter, Hana?

161
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:20,660
I don't have any appetite.

162
00:09:20,726 --> 00:09:23,229
Really? Me too.
My stomach is really upset.

163
00:09:23,296 --> 00:09:24,897
I also get tired easily.

164
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:27,867
And sometimes, it hurts right here.

165
00:09:28,434 --> 00:09:29,435
Dear me.

166
00:09:29,502 --> 00:09:30,536
Come over here.

167
00:09:30,603 --> 00:09:32,371
Sit here on my lap.

168
00:09:32,438 --> 00:09:33,940
Okay!

169
00:09:35,107 --> 00:09:38,477
But didn't you come
to our hospital the other day

170
00:09:38,544 --> 00:09:40,079
for a physical examination?

171
00:09:40,146 --> 00:09:41,814
Nothing was wrong then.

172
00:09:41,881 --> 00:09:43,983
Yes. I was just fine two months ago.

173
00:09:44,050 --> 00:09:46,786
Then maybe it's just your imagination.

174
00:09:46,852 --> 00:09:48,588
I'll prescribe some stomach medicine.

175
00:09:48,654 --> 00:09:49,989
I could use some too.

176
00:09:50,056 --> 00:09:51,490
- Okay.
- Oh, dear. You too?

177
00:09:51,557 --> 00:09:52,825
Stress-induced indigestion.

178
00:09:52,892 --> 00:09:53,893
I know how you feel.

179
00:09:54,493 --> 00:09:57,163
I've dedicated my life as a physician…

180
00:09:57,229 --> 00:09:59,699
to this hospital.

181
00:10:00,466 --> 00:10:02,234
So how dare

182
00:10:02,301 --> 00:10:06,105
that young upstart try and kick me out!

183
00:10:09,241 --> 00:10:10,576
Hana!

184
00:10:26,325 --> 00:10:27,293
You there.

185
00:10:28,761 --> 00:10:29,595
Oh, hey.

186
00:10:30,196 --> 00:10:31,464
Michiko Daimon…

187
00:10:31,530 --> 00:10:32,365
What's wrong?

188
00:10:32,431 --> 00:10:33,366
Are you okay?

189
00:10:33,432 --> 00:10:34,600
What?

190
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:37,903
You're not looking very well.

191
00:10:43,442 --> 00:10:45,111
Dr. Daimon,

192
00:10:45,711 --> 00:10:48,047
you're a lot kinder than you appear.

193
00:10:50,116 --> 00:10:52,485
My husband said it was my imagination.

194
00:10:52,551 --> 00:10:55,521
Have you felt thirsty
or have you had diarrhea lately?

195
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:58,257
Sometimes.

196
00:10:58,924 --> 00:11:02,428
Just in case, we'll run an MRCP
and endoscopic ultrasound.

197
00:11:03,029 --> 00:11:03,929
Got it.

198
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:09,568
If this is a bad disease,

199
00:11:10,469 --> 00:11:12,171
don't tell my husband. Okay?

200
00:11:12,238 --> 00:11:13,072
Why not?

201
00:11:13,706 --> 00:11:16,809
He seems to be having
a lot of trouble right now.

202
00:11:19,211 --> 00:11:22,048
What could be more troubling
than your own wife being sick?

203
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:25,718
Nothing, right?

204
00:11:37,430 --> 00:11:39,765
It has been a while
since you played with us, Akira.

205
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:41,667
He has been acting fishy.

206
00:11:42,268 --> 00:11:45,671
He has been gone forever
doing "research" in Singapore.

207
00:11:46,272 --> 00:11:47,373
Research for what?

208
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,841
What does it matter?

209
00:11:48,908 --> 00:11:50,009
That's fishy.

210
00:11:50,076 --> 00:11:52,211
I bet you're up to something again, Akira.

211
00:11:52,278 --> 00:11:53,679
Who cares about that?

212
00:11:53,746 --> 00:11:55,347
What about you, Michiko?

213
00:11:55,414 --> 00:11:57,616
- He changed the subject!
- That's so fishy.

214
00:11:57,683 --> 00:12:00,386
- You're the fishy one, Michiko.
- What?

215
00:12:00,453 --> 00:12:02,722
I heard she went out for sushi
with Mr. Hachisuka.

216
00:12:02,788 --> 00:12:04,557
Seriously? With Dr. Hachisuka?

217
00:12:04,623 --> 00:12:05,858
A sushi date?

218
00:12:05,925 --> 00:12:08,260
All I did was eat a bunch of sushi.

219
00:12:08,327 --> 00:12:09,462
He didn't eat much though.

220
00:12:09,528 --> 00:12:13,866
Mr. Hachisuka was even nice enough
to give me a gift of sushi too.

221
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:15,568
That sounds serious!

222
00:12:15,634 --> 00:12:18,270
I've never heard a story of romance
with Michiko before!

223
00:12:21,974 --> 00:12:23,142
- Ms. Daimon?
- What?

224
00:12:29,281 --> 00:12:31,383
I accidentally discarded the wrong tile!

225
00:12:31,450 --> 00:12:34,253
Thank you, Michiko! <i>Ron!</i>

226
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:37,356
A nine gates <i>yakuman.</i>

227
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:39,125
- Oh, wow!
- No way!

228
00:12:39,191 --> 00:12:41,927
If I knew this would happen,
I wish you hadn't come back!

229
00:12:41,994 --> 00:12:44,230
Okay! That's 32,000 points!

230
00:12:44,296 --> 00:12:45,598
PROPOSITION FOR IMPROVED PHYSICAL EXAM

231
00:12:45,664 --> 00:12:47,767
I thought you were
Head of Internal Medicine.

232
00:12:48,534 --> 00:12:49,835
What's going on here?

233
00:12:49,902 --> 00:12:51,036
My apologies.

234
00:12:51,103 --> 00:12:56,275
We should be focusing on the work
of the Infection Research Center now.

235
00:12:56,909 --> 00:12:58,811
Instead of worrying about
hospital management,

236
00:12:59,411 --> 00:13:02,248
focus your efforts on Japan's 120 million…

237
00:13:02,848 --> 00:13:03,716
Wait…

238
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:07,686
On the entire population of the world
and saving them!

239
00:13:09,588 --> 00:13:10,723
Doctors!

240
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:20,432
Why is Chief Hachisuka in such a hurry

241
00:13:20,499 --> 00:13:23,068
to get the Infection Research Center open?

242
00:13:23,903 --> 00:13:25,604
He does seem to be in quite a rush.

243
00:13:26,205 --> 00:13:28,541
To be honest, I don't see the point

244
00:13:28,607 --> 00:13:31,410
in preparing for some unknown virus.

245
00:14:04,543 --> 00:14:06,178
Why now?

246
00:14:08,047 --> 00:14:10,416
It's such an important time.

247
00:14:14,453 --> 00:14:18,123
How did I develop such an enormous tumor…

248
00:14:20,159 --> 00:14:22,127
on my pancreas?

249
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:44,583
We will now commence
the online combined meeting

250
00:14:45,184 --> 00:14:48,354
of the Internal Medicine
and Surgery departments!

251
00:14:48,988 --> 00:14:50,089
<i>Glad to have you.</i>

252
00:14:50,589 --> 00:14:54,460
Acting Director Hiruma
will be absent due to poor health.

253
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,462
Let us look at the first case.

254
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:59,665
Is Acting Director Hiruma bedridden?

255
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:02,167
Was he in shock over being kicked out?

256
00:15:02,234 --> 00:15:05,337
Of course not.
He's entertaining people in Okinawa.

257
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:07,840
- Entertaining?
- With Totei University trustees.

258
00:15:08,407 --> 00:15:11,877
It figures Acting Director Hiruma
would be out wrangling.

259
00:15:12,478 --> 00:15:13,746
What's "wrangling"?

260
00:15:14,346 --> 00:15:15,881
Planning his counterattack.

261
00:15:15,948 --> 00:15:18,918
- That's why he's entertaining?
- He's perfectly healthy!

262
00:15:19,518 --> 00:15:20,519
Case two.

263
00:15:22,421 --> 00:15:25,057
Hideo Yoshida, male, age 47.

264
00:15:25,658 --> 00:15:28,527
His diagnosis
is esophagus cancer, stage 3.

265
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:30,496
Let me operate!

266
00:15:30,562 --> 00:15:33,565
There will be no surgery!
We'll administer chemical surgery.

267
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:36,635
The last patient is…

268
00:15:38,170 --> 00:15:41,607
Hanako Hiruma, female, age 62.

269
00:15:42,274 --> 00:15:46,245
Her diagnosis, stage 3
squamous cell carcinoma of the pancreas.

270
00:15:46,745 --> 00:15:49,448
There is a 2.5-centimeter tumor
on the pancreas.

271
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:53,619
It has infiltrated the nerve plexus
around the celiac artery.

272
00:15:53,686 --> 00:15:56,021
Mrs. Hiruma has pancreatic cancer?

273
00:15:56,088 --> 00:15:59,658
Acting Director Hiruma shouldn't be
entertaining in Okinawa now!

274
00:15:59,725 --> 00:16:01,527
You think he doesn't know?

275
00:16:02,361 --> 00:16:05,931
Mrs. Hiruma said not to tell
Acting Director Hiruma.

276
00:16:05,998 --> 00:16:06,999
What?

277
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:10,402
<i>Surgery won't work.</i>

278
00:16:11,036 --> 00:16:13,238
<i>The only choice is chemical surgery.</i>

279
00:16:14,173 --> 00:16:15,074
<i>Hey!</i>

280
00:16:17,009 --> 00:16:18,410
The only choice is surgery!

281
00:16:19,411 --> 00:16:21,080
I can remove it.

282
00:16:22,081 --> 00:16:23,115
<i>Not you again.</i>

283
00:16:24,083 --> 00:16:25,284
<i>You can do it, Dr. Daimon?</i>

284
00:16:25,351 --> 00:16:27,152
You can remove it? What method?

285
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:30,389
Modified DP-CAR.

286
00:16:30,456 --> 00:16:33,726
I'll remove the tumor
while preserving the left gastric artery.

287
00:16:34,226 --> 00:16:35,427
<i>Ridiculous!</i>

288
00:16:35,961 --> 00:16:37,896
Even I couldn't perform that surgery.

289
00:16:37,963 --> 00:16:38,964
Yes, you're right.

290
00:16:39,565 --> 00:16:40,899
You're too sloppy to do it.

291
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:43,569
But I'll remove it with surgery.

292
00:16:43,635 --> 00:16:47,339
If anything happens to Mrs. Hiruma,
your career is finished!

293
00:16:48,273 --> 00:16:49,641
<i>Dr. Daimon.</i>

294
00:16:53,112 --> 00:16:56,715
<i>I will leave this surgery in your hands.</i>

295
00:16:59,418 --> 00:17:00,586
Chief Hachisuka!

296
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:04,256
Are you sure you want to allow surgery?

297
00:17:07,126 --> 00:17:08,961
If you can remove it, then do it!

298
00:17:13,198 --> 00:17:15,768
VIP ROOM B

299
00:17:15,834 --> 00:17:18,103
I'm very sorry about the other day.

300
00:17:19,171 --> 00:17:20,572
Now everyone,

301
00:17:20,639 --> 00:17:23,409
don't stand there
looking like this is a funeral.

302
00:17:24,309 --> 00:17:26,912
I only prescribed medicine
without an exam.

303
00:17:26,979 --> 00:17:30,416
As former Head of Surgery,
I should have proudly offered to operate--

304
00:17:30,482 --> 00:17:31,550
No!

305
00:17:32,151 --> 00:17:33,619
Please, Dr. Ebina,

306
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,922
don't let that bother you.

307
00:17:37,489 --> 00:17:40,559
But Dr. Daimon will perform
the perfect surgery.

308
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:43,662
Dr. Hara and I will be assisting.

309
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:45,431
We will do our very best.

310
00:17:45,998 --> 00:17:47,366
I'm counting entirely on you.

311
00:17:48,467 --> 00:17:50,669
Besides, Dr. Daimon never makes mistakes.

312
00:17:52,337 --> 00:17:55,474
Then would you please sign this?

313
00:17:55,541 --> 00:17:56,375
Certainly.

314
00:17:56,942 --> 00:17:58,210
MASAKO OHMA, NURSE

315
00:17:58,277 --> 00:17:59,344
Excuse me.

316
00:18:02,448 --> 00:18:06,552
Are you sure you don't want to tell
Acting Director Hiruma?

317
00:18:07,119 --> 00:18:10,823
He has been rushing around so busily,
I haven't even seen him.

318
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:12,991
This may be none of my business,

319
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:16,195
but don't you think you should tell him?

320
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:17,529
Forget about it.

321
00:18:18,897 --> 00:18:19,731
Thank you.

322
00:18:19,798 --> 00:18:22,234
Please give this to my husband.

323
00:18:24,002 --> 00:18:25,504
NOTIFICATION OF DIVORCE

324
00:18:25,571 --> 00:18:26,638
Divorce papers?

325
00:18:26,705 --> 00:18:27,539
What?

326
00:18:29,374 --> 00:18:33,078
What Dr. Daimon said the other day
made me think.

327
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:37,216
What could be more troubling
than your own wife being sick?

328
00:18:40,185 --> 00:18:44,890
He wasn't even there
when I gave birth to our daughter.

329
00:18:46,024 --> 00:18:48,794
He was too busy preparing
for the professor election.

330
00:18:51,263 --> 00:18:54,099
I finally realized there's no point
in being with someone

331
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:57,603
who isn't there
during life's important moments.

332
00:19:01,673 --> 00:19:02,808
Once I'm better,

333
00:19:03,942 --> 00:19:07,179
I'll start out again living a new life.

334
00:19:08,614 --> 00:19:09,882
Everyone,

335
00:19:10,849 --> 00:19:12,651
I appreciate your help.

336
00:19:21,193 --> 00:19:25,464
<i>Medical Solutions Headquarters</i>
<i>Chief Hachisuka will now conduct</i>

337
00:19:26,064 --> 00:19:27,633
<i>the chief's rounds.</i>

338
00:19:28,233 --> 00:19:29,067
Tomorrow,

339
00:19:29,134 --> 00:19:30,869
Professor Shelp will arrive in Japan.

340
00:19:31,470 --> 00:19:32,971
Make sure he is welcomed properly!

341
00:19:34,806 --> 00:19:37,476
The Infection Research Center
will be opening at last!

342
00:19:37,543 --> 00:19:40,312
You're really on fire
for your rounds, sir!

343
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:46,118
I wonder if the Hirumas
will really get divorced.

344
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:48,620
Isn't there still time
to talk things over?

345
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:50,122
This is a big problem.

346
00:19:50,722 --> 00:19:53,125
I can't reach
Acting Director Hiruma at all.

347
00:19:53,625 --> 00:19:57,129
Once he starts wrangling,
nothing can stop him.

348
00:19:57,196 --> 00:19:59,398
You surgeons, cut the chatter!

349
00:19:59,898 --> 00:20:01,233
- Yes.
- Sorry.

350
00:20:07,306 --> 00:20:09,208
Join the procession, Dr. Daimon.

351
00:20:09,274 --> 00:20:10,609
I won't.

352
00:20:12,177 --> 00:20:13,412
Good morning.

353
00:20:15,113 --> 00:20:16,014
Hello.

354
00:20:16,615 --> 00:20:17,549
Today is…

355
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:19,952
Mrs. Hiruma's surgery,

356
00:20:20,552 --> 00:20:21,386
isn't it?

357
00:20:21,453 --> 00:20:22,821
What about it?

358
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:25,891
It is an extremely difficult surgery.

359
00:20:26,491 --> 00:20:30,395
I pray for your success, Dr. Daimon.

360
00:20:31,096 --> 00:20:32,064
Really?

361
00:20:32,631 --> 00:20:33,899
How dare you talk like that!

362
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:35,634
Out of the way.

363
00:20:41,506 --> 00:20:42,541
Let's get going.

364
00:20:59,358 --> 00:21:00,592
Welcome back.

365
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:06,798
<i>Welcome home, sir, welcome back home</i>

366
00:21:08,467 --> 00:21:11,570
This is your present, Yui.

367
00:21:11,637 --> 00:21:14,606
- Thank you!
- They're <i>chinsuko</i> cookies.

368
00:21:14,673 --> 00:21:16,475
- And for Dr. Ebina…
- Yes?

369
00:21:18,977 --> 00:21:20,912
- This <i>Shisa</i> statuette.
- Thank you.

370
00:21:20,979 --> 00:21:24,716
And I wanted you to wear
a <i>Kariyushi</i> shirt.

371
00:21:24,783 --> 00:21:26,685
- So I bought you one.
- Thank you.

372
00:21:26,752 --> 00:21:28,053
Here are your presents.

373
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,221
Thank you.

374
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,289
Here.

375
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,659
- Dr. Ebina!
- Yes?

376
00:21:33,725 --> 00:21:35,594
My Okinawa operation

377
00:21:35,661 --> 00:21:40,132
to win over the trustees in
Dr. Hachisuka's camp was a huge success!

378
00:21:40,198 --> 00:21:43,335
Every single night, those trustees--

379
00:21:43,402 --> 00:21:45,037
Actually, Acting Director Hiruma…

380
00:21:45,103 --> 00:21:46,038
What?

381
00:21:46,104 --> 00:21:48,707
- This is from your wife.
- What?

382
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:55,681
NOTIFICATION OF DIVORCE

383
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:59,985
- What kind of joke is this?
- It isn't a joke.

384
00:22:01,687 --> 00:22:03,789
- This is a notification of divorce!
- Yes.

385
00:22:03,855 --> 00:22:05,223
She has even signed it!

386
00:22:05,290 --> 00:22:06,992
She told me to give it to you.

387
00:22:07,059 --> 00:22:08,126
But why?

388
00:22:08,193 --> 00:22:09,861
- Acting Director Hiruma, calm down!
- Okay.

389
00:22:09,928 --> 00:22:11,330
- Actually,
- What?

390
00:22:11,396 --> 00:22:13,665
I have something else
very important to tell you.

391
00:22:13,732 --> 00:22:14,900
What is it?

392
00:22:15,467 --> 00:22:16,601
- Your wife…
- Yes?

393
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:19,371
- She's about to undergo surgery!
- What?

394
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:22,908
Get hold of yourself!

395
00:22:25,177 --> 00:22:26,445
Look at this!

396
00:22:34,586 --> 00:22:37,756
We will now begin
Hanako Hiruma's pancreatectomy…

397
00:22:37,823 --> 00:22:40,559
and left gastric artery
and celiac artery fusion.

398
00:22:40,625 --> 00:22:44,629
BP 106 over 78, pulse 82, normal sinus.

399
00:22:44,696 --> 00:22:45,697
- Scalpel.
- Here.

400
00:22:55,073 --> 00:22:56,575
Pancreatic cancer…

401
00:22:57,242 --> 00:22:59,077
It wasn't stress-related gastritis.

402
00:23:00,078 --> 00:23:01,847
Dr. Daimon found it after running tests.

403
00:23:02,914 --> 00:23:03,982
Hana…

404
00:23:05,951 --> 00:23:06,785
Hana…

405
00:23:09,521 --> 00:23:10,522
- Bovie.
- Here.

406
00:23:22,834 --> 00:23:24,936
Do you really think it will go well?

407
00:23:30,308 --> 00:23:31,510
You can do it!

408
00:23:32,110 --> 00:23:34,646
ANESTHETIZED TIME, SURGERY TIME

409
00:23:44,389 --> 00:23:46,825
It's metastasized to lymph node 14.

410
00:23:47,559 --> 00:23:49,494
- What will you do, Dr. Daimon?
- I can see that.

411
00:23:49,561 --> 00:23:51,863
- I'll dissect the level 3 lymph nodes.
- Got it.

412
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:52,764
- Bovie.
- Here.

413
00:23:52,831 --> 00:23:54,633
I'll assist with the Kocher forceps.

414
00:24:08,413 --> 00:24:09,948
There's number 16 for testing.

415
00:24:10,015 --> 00:24:11,616
- Do a rapid diagnosis.
- Right.

416
00:24:11,683 --> 00:24:12,717
- Take care of this.
- Right.

417
00:24:24,029 --> 00:24:26,665
Dissection of the superior mesenteric
artery nerve plexus complete.

418
00:24:27,265 --> 00:24:28,366
Ablating the tumor now.

419
00:24:28,433 --> 00:24:29,267
- Metz.
- Here.

420
00:24:43,882 --> 00:24:46,318
The tumor has infiltrated
the left gastric artery.

421
00:24:46,384 --> 00:24:48,186
It has spread farther than expected.

422
00:24:48,787 --> 00:24:51,223
Now we can't preserve
the left gastric artery.

423
00:24:51,289 --> 00:24:53,725
What about blood flow
to the stomach and liver?

424
00:24:57,095 --> 00:24:59,130
- Arterial hemorrhaging!
- Suctioning!

425
00:24:59,197 --> 00:25:00,332
- Gauze!
- Here.

426
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,768
The tumor must have weakened
the artery wall!

427
00:25:08,173 --> 00:25:09,808
BP down to the 70s!

428
00:25:11,910 --> 00:25:13,411
- Suction faster!
- Right!

429
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:15,180
- More gauze!
- Right!

430
00:25:19,417 --> 00:25:20,986
Hurry up and find the hemorrhage.

431
00:25:21,052 --> 00:25:22,687
I'm counting on you, Dr. Daimon.

432
00:25:23,688 --> 00:25:25,090
I'm counting on you!

433
00:25:26,291 --> 00:25:28,493
The great Michiko Daimon!

434
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:30,228
Applying pressure. Tupfer forceps.

435
00:25:30,295 --> 00:25:32,731
- Thrombin and fibrinogen, please.
- Right!

436
00:25:33,265 --> 00:25:36,134
I told you it was reckless
to try this surgery!

437
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:38,703
It should have never been performed!

438
00:25:39,738 --> 00:25:42,507
Stop the hemorrhaging and end the surgery!

439
00:26:11,670 --> 00:26:13,371
Chief Hachisuka, are you okay?

440
00:26:14,272 --> 00:26:17,709
If this continues,
she'll go into hemorrhagic shock.

441
00:26:17,776 --> 00:26:20,579
Post-op liver failure
and gastric thrombosis are inevitable!

442
00:26:21,079 --> 00:26:22,614
The pancreatectomy is impossible!

443
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:24,883
You have no choice but to end the surgery!

444
00:26:28,286 --> 00:26:29,321
Dr. Daimon.

445
00:26:29,888 --> 00:26:31,122
Where is it?

446
00:26:33,024 --> 00:26:35,126
- Ten units of red blood cells.
- Right.

447
00:26:36,995 --> 00:26:38,229
Dr. Daimon…

448
00:26:40,398 --> 00:26:41,733
Continue the surgery.

449
00:26:46,538 --> 00:26:48,206
Don't you dare give up.

450
00:26:49,774 --> 00:26:51,276
How could I give up?

451
00:26:53,144 --> 00:26:54,346
Dr. Daimon…

452
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:58,249
Whatever it takes…

453
00:26:59,417 --> 00:27:00,619
Whatever it takes…

454
00:27:02,854 --> 00:27:04,656
save the patient!

455
00:27:08,426 --> 00:27:11,396
I will not fail.

456
00:27:23,141 --> 00:27:24,142
I found it.

457
00:27:24,743 --> 00:27:27,445
The hemorrhaging
is from the inferior phrenic artery.

458
00:27:27,512 --> 00:27:28,546
I'll repair it.

459
00:27:28,613 --> 00:27:30,515
Temporarily block circulation.

460
00:27:30,582 --> 00:27:31,883
- Satinsky clamp.
- Here.

461
00:27:33,284 --> 00:27:34,819
- 4-0 monofilament.
- Here.

462
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,682
BP back up to the 100s.

463
00:28:03,748 --> 00:28:04,716
Thank goodness.

464
00:28:09,387 --> 00:28:12,223
Now is the real challenge, Dr. Daimon.
What will you do?

465
00:28:13,158 --> 00:28:15,126
We'll switch to the Mesenteric approach.

466
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:16,161
- Got it.
- Metz.

467
00:28:16,227 --> 00:28:17,095
Here.

468
00:28:41,519 --> 00:28:42,520
Vitals?

469
00:28:42,587 --> 00:28:46,558
BP 135 over 86, pulse 72, normal sinus.

470
00:28:47,158 --> 00:28:48,359
We're done.

471
00:28:48,426 --> 00:28:50,161
Magnificent operation, Dr. Daimon!

472
00:28:50,228 --> 00:28:52,964
It has been a long time…
I mean, I'm always impressed.

473
00:28:53,031 --> 00:28:55,667
Mrs. Hiruma hung in there well too.

474
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:56,768
That's for sure.

475
00:28:56,835 --> 00:28:58,837
Now she can start living her new life.

476
00:29:01,106 --> 00:29:03,007
Dr. Daimon, well done.

477
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:05,210
- Nice work.
- You too.

478
00:29:27,332 --> 00:29:28,600
Thank goodness.

479
00:29:30,635 --> 00:29:31,636
In any event,

480
00:29:32,237 --> 00:29:34,372
congratulations on the successful surgery.

481
00:29:35,273 --> 00:29:36,341
Dr. Ebina…

482
00:29:36,407 --> 00:29:37,242
Yes?

483
00:29:38,576 --> 00:29:39,577
I am…

484
00:29:40,712 --> 00:29:41,746
going to…

485
00:29:43,314 --> 00:29:44,649
mend my ways.

486
00:29:49,687 --> 00:29:53,958
Until now, I've said
all kinds of rude things to you.

487
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:55,693
I'm sorry.

488
00:29:56,294 --> 00:29:57,428
Don't be silly, sir.

489
00:29:57,495 --> 00:29:58,630
No, you haven't.

490
00:29:58,696 --> 00:30:02,200
I'll spend more time with Hana as well.

491
00:30:02,267 --> 00:30:03,101
Right.

492
00:30:04,269 --> 00:30:10,041
But do you think Hana will forgive me?

493
00:30:10,608 --> 00:30:13,344
- I'm sure she will.
- I hope she does.

494
00:30:13,411 --> 00:30:16,014
Acting Director Hiruma,
Dr. Kuwagata is here.

495
00:30:18,216 --> 00:30:19,384
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

496
00:30:20,685 --> 00:30:23,521
What's your business
with Acting Director Hiruma?

497
00:30:24,355 --> 00:30:27,025
There is something
I would very much like to tell you.

498
00:30:27,091 --> 00:30:27,959
I see.

499
00:30:29,327 --> 00:30:30,795
Will you please leave?

500
00:30:30,862 --> 00:30:31,996
What?

501
00:30:33,598 --> 00:30:35,767
Yes, why don't you leave?

502
00:30:36,701 --> 00:30:37,602
Okay.

503
00:30:38,203 --> 00:30:39,070
Goodbye.

504
00:30:43,241 --> 00:30:44,909
So what is it?

505
00:30:45,577 --> 00:30:48,346
I have something to tell you
about Chief Hachisuka.

506
00:30:48,413 --> 00:30:49,247
Yes?

507
00:30:52,083 --> 00:30:55,453
Sometime a week ago,
he returned to the hospital late at night…

508
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:58,056
and asked me to run tests.

509
00:30:59,724 --> 00:31:00,725
Really?

510
00:31:19,410 --> 00:31:23,181
Compared to before
the chemical surgery HIFU treatment,

511
00:31:24,816 --> 00:31:27,986
the tumor has not shrunk.

512
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:31,990
I guess it means…

513
00:31:33,591 --> 00:31:35,493
it doesn't work on my tumor.

514
00:31:37,729 --> 00:31:38,997
Unfortunately not.

515
00:31:47,739 --> 00:31:51,542
Do not tell anyone about this.

516
00:31:53,611 --> 00:31:54,512
But…

517
00:31:55,513 --> 00:31:59,651
With the Infection Research Center
about to be established,

518
00:32:01,619 --> 00:32:03,621
I don't want to cause confusion.

519
00:32:05,890 --> 00:32:07,125
All right.

520
00:32:09,193 --> 00:32:10,161
Pancreatic cancer?

521
00:32:12,363 --> 00:32:14,465
And since he's pretty young,

522
00:32:15,466 --> 00:32:17,068
it must be progressing rapidly.

523
00:32:19,337 --> 00:32:20,471
Dr. Kuwagata…

524
00:32:22,040 --> 00:32:23,741
By your calculation,

525
00:32:24,943 --> 00:32:28,346
how much longer does he have?

526
00:32:29,647 --> 00:32:31,149
He has six months.

527
00:32:32,684 --> 00:32:34,819
No… Three months.

528
00:32:36,087 --> 00:32:36,988
I see.

529
00:32:38,990 --> 00:32:40,992
But why are you telling me this?

530
00:32:42,527 --> 00:32:45,096
As you told me the other day,

531
00:32:45,697 --> 00:32:50,335
I am originally of a different breed
than Chief Hachisuka.

532
00:32:50,401 --> 00:32:51,235
Yes.

533
00:32:52,770 --> 00:32:55,039
With your assistance,
Acting Director Hiruma,

534
00:32:55,640 --> 00:32:58,977
I would like to become Chief
of the Medical Solutions Headquarters.

535
00:32:59,777 --> 00:33:01,346
With my assistance?

536
00:33:01,846 --> 00:33:02,680
Yes.

537
00:33:03,448 --> 00:33:04,615
Is that right?

538
00:33:05,917 --> 00:33:10,655
You know, you are really very tall.

539
00:33:11,522 --> 00:33:14,058
You may even be taller than Dr. Ebina.

540
00:33:17,295 --> 00:33:20,098
I will stick by your side forever.

541
00:33:31,242 --> 00:33:32,810
Leave this to me.

542
00:33:43,254 --> 00:33:45,857
NOTIFICATION OF DIVORCE

543
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:57,668
You think they'll really get divorced?

544
00:33:58,636 --> 00:34:01,105
I mean, I understand how she feels, but…

545
00:34:02,607 --> 00:34:03,875
I'm sure it will be okay.

546
00:34:04,642 --> 00:34:07,178
Apparently, Acting Director Hiruma said
he would mend his ways

547
00:34:07,779 --> 00:34:09,547
and spend more time with his wife.

548
00:34:10,615 --> 00:34:11,783
Is that right?

549
00:34:16,087 --> 00:34:17,755
- How is she?
- She's stable.

550
00:34:20,124 --> 00:34:23,828
I thought he would mend his ways
if the surgery succeeded. Unbelievable!

551
00:34:24,429 --> 00:34:25,263
What's wrong?

552
00:34:25,329 --> 00:34:29,100
When that Acting Director Hiruma
is offered more power,

553
00:34:29,167 --> 00:34:31,035
he's suddenly filled with energy.

554
00:34:31,102 --> 00:34:33,004
- Yes.
- Just now…

555
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:35,940
Chairman, I'll see you
at the usual place in a moment.

556
00:34:40,778 --> 00:34:41,646
I'm so grateful.

557
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:50,188
He was skipping steps?
Seriously? He's out of his mind!

558
00:34:51,355 --> 00:34:53,791
And he even promised to mend his ways.

559
00:35:09,941 --> 00:35:11,576
You have no choice but to end the surgery!

560
00:35:12,677 --> 00:35:13,511
Where is it?

561
00:35:15,513 --> 00:35:19,183
I will not fail.

562
00:35:56,787 --> 00:35:58,022
Today…

563
00:36:00,525 --> 00:36:02,827
the surgery I witnessed was…

564
00:36:04,195 --> 00:36:07,064
the most magnificent one
that I have ever seen.

565
00:36:10,268 --> 00:36:14,005
Would you like to join me
for a drink at that sushi shop?

566
00:36:19,377 --> 00:36:21,946
Isn't there something else
you should do first?

567
00:36:25,149 --> 00:36:26,450
You've lost your appetite, right?

568
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:30,488
And how long have you had
that pain in your back?

569
00:36:43,401 --> 00:36:45,203
That wasn't the first time, was it?

570
00:36:48,739 --> 00:36:50,808
If you have symptoms, then you must have…

571
00:36:52,777 --> 00:36:54,011
gotten tested.

572
00:36:59,250 --> 00:37:00,851
Let me see all the images.

573
00:37:20,204 --> 00:37:21,272
This is it, huh?

574
00:37:23,574 --> 00:37:24,775
As you know,

575
00:37:25,710 --> 00:37:29,313
I've always been wary of surgeries.

576
00:37:30,881 --> 00:37:33,584
You must have seen too many surgeries
by lousy doctors.

577
00:37:34,819 --> 00:37:35,820
Maybe so.

578
00:37:38,089 --> 00:37:40,591
Just 99% isn't good enough, right?

579
00:37:41,259 --> 00:37:42,727
It must be 100% perfect.

580
00:37:44,428 --> 00:37:46,831
There is no such thing
as a 100% perfect surgery.

581
00:37:48,532 --> 00:37:51,836
That is why I have always promoted
the idea of…

582
00:37:53,704 --> 00:37:54,905
chemical surgery.

583
00:37:57,341 --> 00:38:02,079
As soon as the tumor was found,
I tried HIFU treatment.

584
00:38:04,849 --> 00:38:07,385
But it had no effect on me.

585
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:10,554
So it seems.

586
00:38:14,959 --> 00:38:16,160
Humans…

587
00:38:18,429 --> 00:38:19,597
are weak creatures.

588
00:38:24,735 --> 00:38:28,739
I only realized this
once I myself had become sick.

589
00:38:31,709 --> 00:38:33,344
If that tumor…

590
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:37,548
can be removed through surgery,

591
00:38:39,116 --> 00:38:41,385
then I will pin my hopes
on that ray of light.

592
00:38:46,123 --> 00:38:47,491
Dr. Michiko Daimon…

593
00:38:53,998 --> 00:38:55,166
If possible,

594
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:57,501
I want…

595
00:39:01,238 --> 00:39:03,274
I want you to operate on me!

596
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:27,665
If I enter from the retroperitoneum,

597
00:39:27,732 --> 00:39:31,068
there's a risk of spreading cancer cells
when lifting the pancreas.

598
00:39:33,504 --> 00:39:37,074
What do you think about entering
from the root of the mesentery?

599
00:39:39,410 --> 00:39:42,880
I hate to say it,
but the tumor is in a very bad place.

600
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:48,219
I guess…

601
00:39:49,854 --> 00:39:52,723
even you can't do it, Dr. Daimon.

602
00:40:13,577 --> 00:40:15,212
It will be harder than today's surgery.

603
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:22,987
But…

604
00:40:25,790 --> 00:40:28,993
I'll make it 100% perfect
like you prefer, Dr. Hachisuka.

605
00:40:33,364 --> 00:40:34,265
Dr. Daimon…

606
00:40:39,303 --> 00:40:42,807
I will not fail.

607
00:41:02,393 --> 00:41:05,329
Is Dr. Hachisuka's health really that bad?

608
00:41:06,397 --> 00:41:08,966
He has been working too hard
since last year's pandemic.

609
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:10,768
I heard he hasn't taken a day off.

610
00:41:12,203 --> 00:41:14,605
I guess pushing himself too hard
took its toll.

611
00:41:16,841 --> 00:41:18,375
To be honest,

612
00:41:19,376 --> 00:41:20,611
just between us,

613
00:41:22,213 --> 00:41:25,950
Chief Hachisuka doesn't have
much longer to live.

614
00:41:28,085 --> 00:41:31,155
What about the Infection Research Center
he's opening?

615
00:41:31,222 --> 00:41:32,556
Don't worry.

616
00:41:40,898 --> 00:41:44,635
I have chosen someone
from our own university to become

617
00:41:44,702 --> 00:41:46,904
Chief of the Infection Research Center.

618
00:41:47,905 --> 00:41:49,707
It's nice to meet all of you.

619
00:41:49,773 --> 00:41:50,875
I am Dr. Kuwagata.

620
00:41:51,942 --> 00:41:52,776
Cheers.

621
00:41:54,044 --> 00:41:54,912
Cheers.

622
00:41:55,613 --> 00:41:56,580
Nice to meet you.

623
00:41:57,181 --> 00:41:58,015
Well…

624
00:41:58,082 --> 00:42:00,918
You've already taken on
the attitude of a chief.

625
00:44:12,383 --> 00:44:13,584
This is not good either.

626
00:44:22,026 --> 00:44:22,860
Excuse me.

627
00:44:24,028 --> 00:44:25,996
- Did you forget something?
- No.

628
00:44:28,132 --> 00:44:29,166
Can we talk for a moment?

629
00:44:32,336 --> 00:44:33,604
For decades,

630
00:44:33,671 --> 00:44:37,274
he has been sending masks and soap

631
00:44:38,175 --> 00:44:40,077
to the Middle East and Africa.

632
00:44:41,745 --> 00:44:45,249
Was that before SARS and MARS
became a problem?

633
00:44:45,849 --> 00:44:48,485
That's right. That was over 20 years ago.

634
00:44:49,920 --> 00:44:52,322
The fundamentals of preventing infection

635
00:44:52,389 --> 00:44:53,791
are masks and hand washing.

636
00:44:54,958 --> 00:44:56,860
He knew they would come in handy someday.

637
00:44:58,529 --> 00:44:59,963
But he became depressed

638
00:45:00,464 --> 00:45:04,334
since nobody would wear masks
in those hot climates.

639
00:45:04,935 --> 00:45:06,336
Despite that,

640
00:45:07,071 --> 00:45:09,073
he continued to send masks and soap.

641
00:45:12,776 --> 00:45:15,079
It was only after COVID began to spread…

642
00:45:16,447 --> 00:45:19,016
that those masks that sat
in warehouses for decades

643
00:45:19,083 --> 00:45:20,617
were taken out and used.

644
00:45:20,684 --> 00:45:22,219
PLEASE COME VISIT OUR COUNTRY.

645
00:45:22,286 --> 00:45:24,888
<i>He showed off the photo</i>
<i>from the children in Africa</i>

646
00:45:24,955 --> 00:45:26,657
<i>like a great treasure.</i>

647
00:45:26,724 --> 00:45:28,726
THANKS FOR THE MASKS AND SOAP,
DEAR DOCTOR.

648
00:45:31,895 --> 00:45:35,966
<i>I had never seen Dr. Hachisuka</i>
<i>so happy before.</i>

649
00:45:44,241 --> 00:45:46,410
Now, he's an authority
on infectious diseases.

650
00:45:47,978 --> 00:45:48,912
But that guy,

651
00:45:49,646 --> 00:45:52,916
he doesn't care a bit
about gaining fame or status.

652
00:45:54,685 --> 00:45:55,819
At the core…

653
00:45:55,886 --> 00:45:57,221
At the core,

654
00:45:57,955 --> 00:45:59,123
he's an infection maniac.

655
00:46:03,193 --> 00:46:04,194
I think I see it now.

656
00:46:34,725 --> 00:46:38,395
BEN CASEY
GANNON

657
00:46:40,464 --> 00:46:42,032
Good morning, Michiko.

658
00:46:43,267 --> 00:46:45,035
It's morning already? Good morning.

659
00:46:45,636 --> 00:46:47,638
- Were you up all night?
- Yes.

660
00:46:48,238 --> 00:46:49,640
I'll make some coffee.

661
00:46:55,078 --> 00:46:56,079
Okay!

662
00:46:57,314 --> 00:46:59,950
This is just about 100% perfect.

663
00:47:00,951 --> 00:47:02,553
You sure are zealous.

664
00:47:07,191 --> 00:47:09,626
Who's calling this early in the morning?

665
00:47:39,823 --> 00:47:42,092
That was bad news
first thing in the morning.

666
00:47:42,159 --> 00:47:42,993
What?

667
00:47:43,060 --> 00:47:45,596
There's a new virus spreading.

668
00:47:46,597 --> 00:47:48,432
- A new virus?
- Yes.

669
00:47:48,932 --> 00:47:51,168
I don't know the details.

670
00:47:51,235 --> 00:47:55,806
But apparently, it might be
more contagious than the coronavirus.

671
00:47:56,540 --> 00:47:58,008
Isn't that frightening?

672
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:04,548
Right.

673
00:48:05,148 --> 00:48:09,253
I'll immediately develop measures
to combat this new virus.

674
00:48:10,787 --> 00:48:11,722
What?

675
00:48:13,090 --> 00:48:15,692
Professor Shelp has contracted
the new virus?

676
00:48:19,263 --> 00:48:20,464
And the PCR test results?

677
00:48:23,267 --> 00:48:24,701
Are you absolutely certain?

678
00:48:30,574 --> 00:48:33,310
<i>Attention employees</i>
<i>of Totei University Hospital.</i>

679
00:48:33,377 --> 00:48:34,778
<i>This is Chief Hachisuka.</i>

680
00:48:36,046 --> 00:48:38,348
<i>Infections from the new virus</i>

681
00:48:38,415 --> 00:48:41,618
<i>discovered in Safiristan Kingdom</i>
<i>are spreading.</i>

682
00:48:42,619 --> 00:48:44,054
<i>There is a possibility</i>

683
00:48:44,655 --> 00:48:47,257
<i>that one person has been infected</i>
<i>at this hospital!</i>

684
00:48:52,129 --> 00:48:54,264
I am proclaiming a state of emergency!

685
00:48:54,831 --> 00:48:56,600
<i>Code CBR!</i>

686
00:48:56,667 --> 00:48:58,468
<i>Code CBR!</i>

687
00:48:58,535 --> 00:49:01,238
<i>Code CBR! I repeat…</i>

688
00:49:02,572 --> 00:49:06,209
There is a possibility
of an infection here from the new virus.

689
00:49:06,977 --> 00:49:11,581
The Infection Research Center
is off limits!

690
00:49:11,648 --> 00:49:13,150
Code CBR!

691
00:49:13,750 --> 00:49:15,085
Code CBR!

692
00:49:15,152 --> 00:49:20,257
<i>I repeat, code CBR!</i>

693
00:50:50,714 --> 00:50:52,582
I cannot allow
anyone else to become infected!

694
00:50:52,649 --> 00:50:54,618
I bet he's infected.

695
00:50:54,684 --> 00:50:56,520
<i>He's ignoring his own illness</i>

696
00:50:56,586 --> 00:50:58,121
<i>to save the infected patient.</i>

697
00:50:58,188 --> 00:50:59,222
<i>I won't give up either.</i>

698
00:50:59,289 --> 00:51:01,291
I'll make this a 100% perfect surgery!

699
00:51:03,293 --> 00:51:04,494
Hacchi!

700
00:51:04,561 --> 00:51:05,395
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
